{
  "$comment": [
    "Vendor sources for each STM32 family, as evidence rather than convention.",
    "",
    "A STM32Cube<Family> repository is a meta-repository: the HAL driver and the",
    "CMSIS device headers \u2014 which is where the startup assembly and system file",
    "live \u2014 are git submodules pointing at repositories of their own. Cloning the",
    "Cube repository therefore does not get you the HAL, and nothing that compiles",
    "against a peripheral comes with it.",
    "",
    "The Nucleo BSP is a third repository, on `main` for every family checked here",
    "even where the Cube repository itself is on `master`, and its name is not",
    "derivable: stm32f0xx-nucleo-32-bsp, p-nucleo-wb55-nucleo-bsp and",
    "nucleo-c031c6-bsp are all real and none of them is <family>-nucleo-144-bsp.",
    "",
    "Verified 2026-09-30 by reading .gitmodules from each Cube repository's",
    "default branch, and by confirming that cmsis_device_f4 carries",
    "Include/stm32f4xx.h, Source/Templates/gcc/startup_stm32f407xx.s and",
    "Source/Templates/system_stm32f4xx.c, and that stm32f4xx_hal_driver carries",
    "Inc/ and Src/.",
    "",
    "A preset is built from these: the CMSIS core headers come from the Cube",
    "repository itself (Drivers/CMSIS/Core/Include), which is why the Cube",
    "repository is still needed even though the HAL is not in it."
  ],
  "verified": "2026-09-30",
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "STM32H7",
      "core": "cortex-m7",
      "cube": {
        "git": "https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeH7",
        "branch": "master"
      },
      "hal": {
        "git": "https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32h7xx_hal_driver",
        "branch": "master"
      },
      "cmsis_device": {
        "git": "https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/cmsis_device_h7",
        "branch": "master"
      },
